# Coach speech (Italian): the appraisal after the game (src/coach/appraisal.cpp).
# Same keys and variants as assets/coach/speech/en/appraisal.lang (its header documents every placeholder).
# The appraisal is always positive and never blames. The coach says "tu"; the player's gender is
# unknown: no adjective or participle agrees with the player (no "bravo", "sei pronto", "eri
# vicino"). Use avere ("hai vinto", "ce l’avevi quasi fatta"), "stavi vincendo", nouns and impersonal
# phrasing ("sei all’altezza", "la vittoria era vicina").
#
# Names inserted by {text}, {theme}, {level}, {opening} (written to fit every line that inserts them):
#   appraisal.phase.*   with their article ("l’apertura", "il mediogioco", "il finale"); after a
#                       preposition use the forms of common.lang: "{text:in}" = "nell’apertura";
#                       "è stat{text:o}" agrees with the phase.
#   appraisal.reason.*  a complement after "Patta, {text}." ("per ripetizione").
#   theme.*             an infinitive phrase ("guardare tutta la scacchiera prima di muovere"), said
#                       after a colon or after "allenati a" (no theme starts with a- : no "ad").
#   appraisal.level.*   the coach page's level name in « », always after "livello":
#                       "al livello «Principiante»".
#   {opening:def}       the opening's name with its article ("la Partita italiana") after a verb;
#                       {opening} alone (the citation name) after a colon.
# Accuracy: "{acc:percent}" = "85%" (spoken "ottantacinque per cento"), never after an article or
# "di" (Italian would elide: "dell’85%"): after a colon, or "{acc:percent} di precisione".
# Move numbers: "alla mossa {n}", "Mossa {n}:" (no ordinals, no article before a number).

